# Every secret this project needs, in one file.
#
# The real one is secrets.env, beside this file: gitignored, never committed,
# and kept in the password vault, as in the sibling projects. A lost checkout
# plus secrets.env from the vault is a working setup again. This repository
# is public; nothing below ever goes into a tracked file.
#
# Agents never read secrets.env, and never run the targets that do
# (CLAUDE.md, section 6; .claude/settings.json).
#
# In order, once:
#
#   make release-keygen        make the release key: the private half here,
#                              the public half in release-key.pub
#   (save secrets.env in the vault; commit release-key.pub by pull request)
#   make release-send-secret   the private half to the GitHub Actions secret
#   make release-status        is everything in place? says what is not
#
# Then every merge to main that changes the program is a signed release
# (docs/10-install-update-and-releases.md).


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RELEASE: the key every release is signed with. Becomes the GitHub Actions
# secret RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY, and goes nowhere else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The standard base64 of the 64-byte Ed25519 private key. Written by
# make release-keygen; never typed. Losing it means the next release can't be
# signed with a key the installed copies trust, and each computer must then
# be updated once by hand (docs/10, "The release signing key").
RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY_B64=
